From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 02:00:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] 031 (TKFillet): corner of two fillets that end on the
 sharp edges between them

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreThreeCorner, the !inters branch. When the fillets on both
sides of a sharp (not filleted) edge both end ON that edge at different points (a
vertical edge fillet running into two concave chamfer faces, filleted together with
the chamfers' miter edge), the stock code cut every stripe back to one common setback
distance: the nearer fillet's end left the edge, the corner got a G0 batten across
each chamfer face and the GeomPlate patch folded along it (owner's part: creases up
to 92 deg, edge tolerance 6.4e-2, 16.7 deg G1 break to the fillets).

Now, for rolling-ball fillets only (FilSpine), when every neighbour of such stripes is
such an edge and each stripe is the farther or the nearer one on both of its edges:
- the nearer stripe keeps its end; the corner border to it is the piece of the edge
  between the two ends (the contact set of the rolling ball on the edge);
- the farther stripe is set back by the gap along the edge (setback vertex blend,
  Varady-Rockwood CAD 1997), its border line on the face is continued to the edge and
  is a G1 border of the plate.
Otherwise (and for chamfers) the stock path is taken unchanged.

Owner's part: valid, BOP check OK, edge tol 7.2e-3, G1 break to the fillets 1.2 deg,
no folds. Identity: DRAW blend group 475/475 byte-identical; own sweep of 9870
fillet/chamfer operations on 17 shapes differs only in the flanked-edge corners
(70 cases, all better by validity/check/folds/G1/tolerance).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
